---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Terms of Service — ${site.name}`}
  description={`The plain-language terms for using ${site.name}'s website.`}
  locale="en"
  path="/terms/"
>
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: August 25, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      These are the plain-language terms for using this website
      ({site.url}). This isn't a contract for our consulting services —
      that's a separate conversation we'll have directly with you. This
      page just covers the website itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Using this site</h2>
    <p>
      You're welcome to browse this site, read the blog, and get in touch
      through the contact form. Don't use it to do anything illegal, try to
      break it, or scrape it for spam.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantees from the content</h2>
    <p>
      The blog posts and service pages on this site are general information,
      not a guarantee of specific results for your business. Every business
      is different, and what worked for one isn't automatically going to
      work the same way for another.
    </p>

    <h2>Ownership</h2>
    <p>
      The content, design, and writing on this site belong to {site.name}
      unless otherwise noted. Don't copy it wholesale and pass it off as
      your own.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside links</h2>
    <p>
      If we link to another website, we're not responsible for what's on
      it. Once you click away from our site, their rules apply, not ours.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms occasionally. If we do, we'll update the
      date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Reach us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
